    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0223" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg119"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 808.00/1651.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-05-09T18:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1913—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Both Houses have passed resolutions expressing appreciation, to be communicated
                    to you through the Chinese Minister at Washington.</p>
                <p>In celebration of the recognition of the Republic by the United States,
                    deputations from commercial and other organizations and pupils and teachers from
                    the principal schools paraded with American and Chinese flags and called at the
                    Legation yesterday. They requested me to convey to the Government and people of
                    the United States their sincere gratitude for its friendly action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
